{"step_index":887,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:55:00Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-25T18:25:00+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-25T18:25:00+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/server.py`\nTotal Lines: 69\nTotal Bytes: 2565\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"\n2: server.py — Local HTTP Server & Execution API for Code Flow Visualizer\n3: Serves static frontend assets from `app_build/` and exposes `/api/validate` & `/api/trace`.\n4: Zero external dependencies or AI APIs required.\n5: Run: python server.py\n6: Open: http://127.0.0.1:8080\n7: \"\"\"\n8: \n9: import json\n10: import os\n11: from http.server import HTTPServer, SimpleHTTPRequestHandler\n12: from app_build.engine import trace_python_program, validate_python_support\n13: from app_build.explainer import generate_step_explanation\n14: \n15: PORT = 8080\n16: BASE_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n17: APP_BUILD_DIR = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"app_build\")\n18: \n19: \n20: class VisualizerRequestHandler(SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n21:     def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n22:         super().__init__(*args, directory=APP_BUILD_DIR, **kwargs)\n23: \n24:     def _send_json(self, status_code: int, data: dict):\n25:         payload = json.dumps(data).encode(\"utf-8\")\n26:         self.send_response(status_code)\n27:         self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n28:         self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(payload)))\n29:         self.end_headers()\n30:         self.wfile.write(payload)\n31: \n32:     def do_GET(self):\n33:         if self.path == \"/favicon.ico\":\n34:             self.send_response(204)\n35:             self.end_headers()\n36:             return\n37:         if self.path.startswith(\"/app_build/\"):\n38:             self.path = self.path[len(\"/app_build\") :]\n39:         super().do_GET()\n40: \n41:     def do_POST(self):\n42:         length = int(self.headers.get(\"Content-Length\", 0))\n43:         raw_body = self.rfile.read(length).decode(\"utf-8\") if length > 0 else \"{}\"\n44:         body = json.loads(raw_body)\n45: \n46:         if self.path == \"/api/validate\":\n47:             code = body.get(\"code\", \"\")\n48:             ok, msg, ln = validate_python_support(code)\n49:             self._send_json(200, {\"ok\": ok, \"errorMessage\": msg, \"errorLine\": ln})\n50:             return\n51: \n52:         if self.path == \"/api/trace\":\n53:             code = body.get(\"code\", \"\")\n54:             custom_input = body.get(\"input\", \"\")\n55:             result = trace_python_program(code, custom_input)\n56:             steps = result.get(\"steps\", [])\n57:             for idx, st in enumerate(steps):\n58:                 prev_st = steps[idx - 1] if idx > 0 else None\n59:                 st[\"explanations\"] = generate_step_explanation(st, prev_st)\n60:             self._send_json(200, result)\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":888,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:55:00Z","input_tokens":3250,"cache_read_tokens":97624,"output_tokens":3233,"content":"### Phase 5 Implementation Complete: Test and Polish\n\nAll Phase 5 requirements have been implemented, verified, and polished across the offline **Code Flow Visualizer** without external APIs or paid dependencies.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Completed Enhancements\n\n#### 1. Step Restoration & Deterministic Time-Travel Verification\n- **Immutable Snapshot Architecture**: Every execution step created by [engine.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.js) records an isolated snapshot of:\n  - `beforeVars`: exact variable dictionary before the step executes.\n  - `callStack` & `scopeFrames`: cloned local and global frames with variable bindings.\n  - `memoryModel`: heap object addresses (`@0x2000`, `@0x3000`), object types, and element references.\n  - `condition`: left operand, operator, right operand, and boolean result.\n  - `loop`: current iteration, active index, element value, and total iterations.\n  - `teachingSubsteps`: pre-calculated beginner teaching substeps.\n- **Backward & Forward Navigation**:\n  - In [app.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js), `goToPrevSubstep()`, `goToNextSubstep()`, and `goToStep()` render state directly from the targeted snapshot without state mutation leakage. Navigating backward instantly restores the exact variable values, active line highlight, and memory model.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Every Iteration and Condition Verified\n- **Loop Tracking**:\n  - `LOOP_ITER` highlights the active index and value in the visual loop strip, while animating the pointer indicator to track the element currently being processed.\n  - `LOOP_END` displays the completion banner indicating that all iterations are finished.\n- **Branch & Decision Gate**:\n  - For `if c >= ans:`, the visual gate shows current values, the comparison (e.g. `-2 >= -2` or `1 >= -2`), the True/False outcome badge (`.decision-badge.is-true` / `.decision-badge.is-false`), and marks which branch executes vs. skipped.\n  - For `if c < 0:`, when the running su\n<truncated 1330 bytes>\n Reduced-Motion Accessibility\n- **Speed Controller (`⚡ Speed`)**:\n  - Added in the top navigation bar. Cycles between:\n    - **`1x`**: Standard speed (1200ms step interval, 1.0x animation factor).\n    - **`1.5x`**: Faster speed (750ms step interval, 0.65x animation factor).\n    - **`2x`**: Rapid speed (450ms step interval, 0.4x animation factor).\n    - **`0.5x`**: Slow teaching speed (2200ms step interval, 1.8x animation factor).\n  - In [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css#L52-L54), CSS variable `--anim-speed-factor` dynamically scales all UI animation durations:\n    - `.var-box-value` (value entry pop)\n    - `.var-box-card.is-updated` (green pulse)\n    - `.anim-source-val` and `.anim-move-arrow` (number moving into box)\n    - `.zero-reset-box` (negative value reset pop)\n    - `.decision-badge` (condition outcome pop)\n    - `.loop-return-banner` and `.loop-pointer-indicator`\n- **Reduced Motion & Accessibility**:\n  - **Manual Toggle**: `✨ Animations: ON` / `⚡ Animations: OFF` button adds `body.no-animations` to disable all transitions and keyframe animations immediately.\n  - **Automatic Detection**: On load, `initAccessibility()` detects the user's OS accessibility settings via `window.matchMedia(\"(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\")`.\n  - **CSS Fallback**: Added `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` in [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css#L1315-L1325) overriding animation and transition durations to `0.001s`.\n\n---\n\n#### 5. 100% Offline & Zero API Calls Confirmed\n- No AI model endpoints, remote dependencies, API keys, or cloud services are invoked.\n- The entire application runs natively in any modern web browser by opening [app_build/index.html](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html), or locally using Python's standard library via [server.py](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/server.py).","thinking":"Focusing on the requirement to verify \"Previous Step\" and \"Next Step\" functionality for correct value restoration. This necessitates rigorous testing across different scenarios to ensure data integrity during navigation. Plan is to systematically test these functions with varied inputs to confirm the expected behavior.\n\n\nFocused verification of step navigation and value restoration by analyzing the immutable data snapshots. The system captures the state of variables, call stacks, memory models, conditions, loops, and teaching substeps at each execution step. This data is leveraged to accurately restore the application's state when navigating between steps.\n\n\nAnalyzing Kadane's algorithm, specifically the condition `if c >= ans` and the negative reset `if c < 0`. Test cases will systematically cover mixed, all-negative, all-positive, and single-element inputs to evaluate the algorithm's behavior. The negative reset is crucial for handling all-negative input.\n\nThe goal is to verify the correct sum is identified and step navigation restores the correct `ans` and `c` values at each iteration. All-negative inputs present a key test because Kadane's algorithm must correctly identify the least-negative number as the maximum subarray. Initial and accumulated values need to be validated on restoration.\n\n\nAdding animation speed controls involves dynamic CSS property modification to scale animation durations based on user selection. Reduced motion features use a CSS class toggle and media query for accessibility compliance, disabling animations automatically when the user's preference is detected. The application's core functionality is verified to work fully offline, without any external dependencies.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
